{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption","id":985641,"title":"About redemption","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T13:42:42-07:00","id":985641,"title":"About redemption","content":"Hi !<br /> <br /> Here again for a metaphysical question. What happens to the inverted Avatar of a Nephandus ? I read the Book of Madness and found very few things on the matter. It states though that Nephandi could die but would be reincarnated into Widderslaints. Is there no possibility for redemption then ?<br /> <br /> As far as I understand it, there is none. But I find it quite odd. The World of Darkness is a decaying world, tainted by corruption and depression. But Mages are the symbol of hope of that world. This is also a mystical world where the notions of fate and freewill are debated on a daily basis. I find it hard to believe that no hope of redemption is possible even in the most extreme cases. The World of Darkness seems balanced to me. Far from mitigated, but balanced nonetheless. Evil is more evil than in our world, and good is more good. Redemption is a whole theme of many chronicles of the WoD, even official ones such as the Red Sign for exemple.<br /> <br /> The choice of falling to the demon is a choice of the human being. It changes the Avatar but, why would it be impossible that in a next life, a Widderslainte choses to betray his demon to make his Avatar whole again ? After all, nor the Avatar nor the Widderslainte had a word about it in the first place. Betrayings could go either way don't you think ? Before the question is asked, I'm not sure I'm even talking about an actual Nephandus, but rather talking about the next lives of said Nephandus.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:10:17-07:00","id":985664,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatos book mentions Senex (the Euthanatos Archmaster) having an apprentice called Amanda who seems to be a Widderslainte. He apparently doesn't see that as an issue.<br /> <br /> (I get the feeling it's referencing something I haven't read)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:17:16-07:00","id":985670,"title":"","content":"The knowledge held by mages that an inverted avatar is beyond help could simply be false knowledge.<br /> <br /> That would be dark and furthering the nephandic goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> I rule nothing out, everything is possible when I am the ST. But possible means not necessarily easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:39:58-07:00","id":985686,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, it could just be a matter of practicality. Repairing an inverted avatar is more difficult and less sure than simply destroying it via Gilgul. Faced with the risks, most people choose the latter.<br /> <br /> If this carries on for long enough it simply becomes an accepted fact that Inverted Avatars cannot be fixed. When originally it was Inverted Avatars cannot be fixed <i>practically.</i> To begin with.<br /> <br /> I'm relatively sure given enough time and effort, an inverted avatar could be knocked back into the right shape again. Possibly a bit worse for wear but eh. It would take Spirit 5 at least. Possibly Entropy of some sort since we're dealing with destinies and whatnot. Perhaps time? To reach back into the past and retroactively kill the original nephandus who corrupted it before it can be corrupted? Causing the current widderslainte to be fixed.<br /> <br /> Dunno really.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's also a potential element of risk, a la Avatar the Last Airbender, in that using your avatar to try to de-invert theirs you open yourself up to inversion yourself as they try to bring you with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:15:30-07:00","id":985710,"title":"","content":"I remember reading that there was a narrow window of redemption for an avatar that was recently inverted. A barrabi with a newly inverted Avatar can revert is the mage is killed within a number of days dependant on the avatar strength. This is one of the reasons why Euthanatoi are so desperate to kill newly turned Nephandi.<br /> <br /> I also remember reading somewhere a case in which a Widderslainte willing gave themselves up for gilgul after learning of what they were, and when the avatar was removed and destroyed it did not resemble that or an inverted one, as though the act of rejecting the inversion she was given and willingly sacrificing herself was enough to redeem her. Unfortunately though, the damage of gilgul had rendered such a transformation moot. Perhaps then if a Widderslainte took their own life with the exact same intention and real feeling of desperate desire for redemption may allow the avatar to revert back when it reincarnates next.<br /> <br /> That being said, it may not work depending on how ancient the avatar is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:23:35-07:00","id":985909,"title":"","content":"It might be a very interesting story hook, dropping the possibility of a ritual that could reverse Nephandism. Or, better yet, a kind of <i>Anti-Caul</i>.<br /> <br /> Consider the functional opposite of a Nephandus labyrinth, at center of which stands a door plated in gold. Light pours out when it opens, and anyone who enters is surrounded by a swarm of angels, resplendent in their finery. An uncorrupted Mage is promptly and gently escorted back out if they wander in - there is nothing more that this host can do to help the Mage on their journey to Ascension. But if a Nephandus walks (or is forced) inside, they are immediately confronted, and the door slams shut.<br /> <br /> Just as with a Caul, the Nephandus faces a choice. Indeed, the angels make the choice transparent, so that there is no misunderstanding (for unlike the demonic Cauls, this Anti-Caul is honest and forthright about its purpose). The dark Mage may do one of three things. One, they may stay still, moving neither forward or backward. For so long as they don't move, the angels will wait. Two, the Nephandus turns to run away, at which point they are promptly destroyed on the spot, burned to atoms by holy fire. But Three, the Nephandus may move forward, and accept the angel's blessing. This is the choice the angels encourage, which the whole host beckoning with sweet words, with promises of redemption and renewal.<br /> <br /> Should the Nephandus step forward, the angels will carry them up (at this point, while the angel's hands are gentle as a whisper, there is no escaping them; the choice has been made). They carry the Mage forward into blinding light. Divine fire burns their soul - for indeed, pain is a necessary part of becoming better - until the taint is boiled away. Their flesh is unraveled, and purged of infection. And their mind is taken apart by delicate, expert hands. Their consciousness is flooded by visions of nobility, virtue, love, and hope. In that moment, the Nephandus is driven sane, their broken heart, soul, and/or Avatar is put back together, the right <i>way</i>. This process, all told, can take some time, depending on the severity of the Nephandus's sins. The angels are not hasty, but treat each transgression in turn. If it takes five hours or five hundred years, they will keep the soul to the purifying flame, until the world-hating malice is no more.<br /> <br /> And when their body has been reassembled, they are annointed with sweet-smelling oils, and dressed in fine clothing. A fine costume, befitting a refined and positive version of their Paradigm. Their hunger is sated by sweet fruit, and their thirst by rich milk or wine. And songs of hope and good-tidings are sung into their ear. And at last, with their work complete, they usher the newly restored Mage through the threshold, to rejoin the world and contribute to its goodness. While what exactly is &quot;good&quot; is up to the Mage's Paradigm, they nonetheless are driven towards Ascension, rather than Descent.<br /> <br /> Or, so it is rumored...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:42:46-07:00","id":986312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=985909#post985909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be a very interesting story hook, dropping the possibility of a ritual that could reverse Nephandism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you said it, that was totally something I thought. I asked about it here to be sure it would not be inconsistent with the WoD. I was not sure about the scenario yet. I have some ideas about exploiting the Widderslainte concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T19:28:50-07:00","id":986518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=985909#post985909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be a very interesting story hook, dropping the possibility of a ritual that could reverse Nephandism. Or, better yet, a kind of <i>Anti-Caul</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, so it is rumored...</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of something that I read about the Ahl-i-Batin. Something to the effect of how they're somehow attuned at traversing labyrinths, even to the point of being able to come out the other side of the Black Spiral unscathed. However, because they are particularly ant-Nephandi, it's also likely that the Batini that come out the other end <i>not</i> unscathed are actually deep cover agents. They are, after all, the Subtle Ones. Who knows? Maybe with all of their obsession with labyrinths and Nephandi they've discovered things pointing to a way back.<br /> <br /> I'd say that if you wanted to run a Nephandus redemption arc, look at including the Ahl-i-Batin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:04:51-07:00","id":986581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986518#post986518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This reminds me of something that I read about the Ahl-i-Batin. Something to the effect of how they're somehow attuned at traversing labyrinths, even to the point of being able to come out the other side of the Black Spiral unscathed. However, because they are particularly ant-Nephandi, it's also likely that the Batini that come out the other end <i>not</i> unscathed are actually deep cover agents. They are, after all, the Subtle Ones. Who knows? Maybe with all of their obsession with labyrinths and Nephandi they've discovered things pointing to a way back.<br /> <br /> I'd say that if you wanted to run a Nephandus redemption arc, look at including the Ahl-i-Batin.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good advice, thank you. I have their lost path supplement but actually never read it ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T00:01:01-07:00","id":986610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986581#post986581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a good advice, thank you. I have their lost path supplement but actually never read it ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Eehhhh...I don't want to say &quot;Don't&quot;, but...<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way. Lost Paths outright states that the Ahl-i-Batin invented Islam. As in, they tormented the Prophet Muhammad with visions and voices, and wouldn't stop until he agreed to write the &quot;revelations&quot; down and make a religion out of them.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not a Muslim. But if I were, I'd be pretty insulted by such a treatment of Islam. And all in service to an overly intricate backstory for the Batini. I don't know, the Ahl-i-Batin just rub me the wrong way for reasons that I can't quite put into words, and Lost Paths doesn't help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:09:24-07:00","id":986642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986610#post986610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it this way. Lost Paths outright states that the Ahl-i-Batin invented Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misremembering. It says they claim they created it. Also even their story is a tad more complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:56:00-07:00","id":986654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986642#post986642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're misremembering. It says they claim they created it. Also even their story is a tad more complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But just them <i>claiming</i> to have invented it is problematic, no? If their claim is true (in the way that anything in Mage can be considered &quot;true&quot;), then my above point still stands. And if their claim is false, then it points to some colossal hubris on their part.<br /> <br /> On further reflection, the latter seems more likely. They are the special snowflake Craft above all other special snowflake groups. Origins purported to predate the known universe, being a combination of two existing Traditions, have access to Arcane 6+, claims to be uniquely qualified to fight the Nephandi, being more &quot;subtle&quot; than everyone else, and their tendency to crib Practices from several other groups (alchemy, Kabbala, dervishism, etc.). Their hilariously vague group goal of &quot;UNITY(!!!)&quot;. Even their limitation - not just an unwillingness, but a <i>metaphysical inability</i> to learn Entropy - is special snowflake in its own way.<br /> <br /> I think I've figured out why I don't like the Ahl-i-Batin. They are the smuggest, most Mary Sue of Mage groups, and it makes me want to punch them collectively in the face. You're free to disagree, but that's just how I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:17:33-07:00","id":986670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986654#post986654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And if their claim is false, then it points to some colossal hubris on their part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... they are the group who claim they can waltz into a Caul and come out just fine; and also weren't some of the worst Nephandi explicitly former Batini...<br /> <br /> More broadly the problematic aspect of the Batini is basically the same problem all the Traditions have to varying degrees. They imply that sleeper religions are just simplified copies of the real thing.<br /> <br /> In any case, when is this ever going to come up? Unless you actually play a game where you actually meet the prophet, in which case you're already in really weird territory anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:12:13-07:00","id":986689,"title":"","content":"I get that it's your personal feelings, Bluecho, but you could make a Mary-Sue list like that for any of the Traditions (which the Ahl-i-Batin were until relatively recently). Hermetics claiming to have started the Council and having True Names as a magic shield against sympathetic magic, can't stop saying &quot;bani&quot;, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:22:48-07:00","id":986714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986654#post986654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. But just them <i>claiming</i> to have invented it is problematic, no? If their claim is true (in the way that anything in Mage can be considered &quot;true&quot;), then my above point still stands. And if their claim is false, then it points to some colossal hubris on their part.<br /> <br /> On further reflection, the latter seems more likely. They are the special snowflake Craft above all other special snowflake groups. Origins purported to predate the known universe, being a combination of two existing Traditions, have access to Arcane 6+, claims to be uniquely qualified to fight the Nephandi, being more &quot;subtle&quot; than everyone else, and their tendency to crib Practices from several other groups (alchemy, Kabbala, dervishism, etc.). Their hilariously vague group goal of &quot;UNITY(!!!)&quot;. Even their limitation - not just an unwillingness, but a <i>metaphysical inability</i> to learn Entropy - is special snowflake in its own way.<br /> <br /> I think I've figured out why I don't like the Ahl-i-Batin. They are the smuggest, most Mary Sue of Mage groups, and it makes me want to punch them collectively in the face. You're free to disagree, but that's just how I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point and I keep an open-mind. But I agree with Haldir2012. You can say that about most Traditions. Euthanatoi toy with the Realm of the Dead and I'm pretty sure Choristers believe they created monotheism. Colossal hubris here too. More generally speaking, Mages tend to say everything came from them in the first place. Sometimes it's true but I would say that most of the time it is not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:03:08-07:00","id":986792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=986714#post986714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get your point and I keep an open-mind. But I agree with Haldir2012. You can say that about most Traditions. Euthanatoi toy with the Realm of the Dead and I'm pretty sure Choristers believe they created monotheism. Colossal hubris here too. More generally speaking, Mages tend to say everything came from them in the first place. Sometimes it's true but I would say that most of the time it is not...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Order of Hermes are all about how they are the only reason that people do magic in a unified way at all. They invented the sphere classification system and imposed it on to all the others until it just became easier for communications sake just to go with it.<br /> <br /> Heck the Verbena too claim that all school of magic, including the Order of Reason and later the Technocracy, came from the descendants of the Wyck, and thus their ancient rituals are the roots of all magic that has come after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:57:22-07:00","id":988290,"title":"","content":"Let's say it is like after healing an addiction, the temptaion to fall again remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:52:24-07:00","id":988931,"title":"","content":"This thread is really interesting and has some nice ideas and information!<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear some opinions on how to roleplay or represent the experience of the widderslainte. How does having been born with an inverted Avatar feels? Is there a Flaw for it in some book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:11:05-07:00","id":988991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=988931#post988931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is really interesting and has some nice ideas and information!<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear some opinions on how to roleplay or represent the experience of the widderslainte. How does having been born with an inverted Avatar feels? Is there a Flaw for it in some book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, given that neither White Wolf nor Onyx Path encourage the playing of Nephandi, Barrabus or otherwise. So there likely isn't any Flaw that replicates the full Widderslainte experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:35:35-07:00","id":988999,"title":"","content":"The closest you could probably come is &quot;Dark Fate: You're a widderslainte and doomed to succumb.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:48:35-07:00","id":989030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/985641-about-redemption?p=988999#post988999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest you could probably come is &amp;quot;Dark Fate: You're a widderslainte and doomed to succumb.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Close enough to try it.<br /> That is actually a very good (if not the best) explanation for Dark Fate that I read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:09:03-07:00","id":989059,"title":"","content":"Dark Fate makes sense. Anyone had an actual experience with a PC or NPC <i>widderslainte?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:44:31-07:00","id":989238,"title":"","content":"I do not think I would advise nor accept a player with a widdlerslainte character in my chronicle. A npc, I would though. It can make interesting sessions. But nephandi are too twisted to accept it from players... Dealing with maniacs is one thing, playing with them is another ^^<br /> <br /> And what differentiate players from the ST is the distance between the real person and the character. At least that's my opinion. And even in that case, I would suggest the horror rather than describing it flat (for my own sanity ^^).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:14:43-07:00","id":989333,"title":"","content":"If you wabt to try it, there was an article wayback on Anders Mage Page:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020804011135/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/redempt.txt\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020804011135/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/redempt.txt\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020804011135/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/redempt.txt\" target=\"_blank\"> http://web.archive.org/web/20020804011135/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/redempt.txt </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:58:36-07:00","id":989372,"title":"","content":"In an Ascension crossover fic I've been writing off and on there's a widderslaint character. One of the major plot points will be the bindings keeping her on the straight and narrow fading, forcing the protagonist Euthanatos to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:20:09-07:00","id":989451,"title":"","content":"Im not one to say anything is impossible in Mage, given the right Spheres, knowledge, time, and resources anything is possible. However given the presentation of going through the Cauls I can only view undoing its effects as a massive undertaking. Much of it relies heavily on ST adjudication (like most things in Mage).<br /> <br /> As an ST you would have to decide the following<ul><li>Is it even possible to save the Avatar once it has gone through the Cauls, or are the Euthanatoi right?</li> <li>If it is possible what Spheres are required and at what levels (below are my thoughts in that regard, I'm not saying all the Spheres below would be required just my thoughts on what ones might be needed)<ul><li>Spirit 5: is a definite, since that covers destroying Avatars and manipulating ephemera</li> <li>Time 3: You might need to 'rollback' to borrow a computer term. Basically rewinding to a point before the Avatar was inverted/corrupted</li> <li>Life 2/3: You might need to affect the Mage's body as well as her Avatar. Additionally you may need to heal the physical damage caused by the ritual</li> <li>Mind 3/4: You might have to heal and repair the mental trauma and scars caused by the trip through the Caul or manipulate the connection between the Mage and their Avatar</li> <li>Prime 3: You might have to draw and feed quintessence into the effect, acting as a constant flow of purifying energy</li> <li>Arch-Spirit (6+): If such vaunted power exists in you game, then it likely can undo the effect at some level. Requiring it could explain why everyone thinks the Cauls are permanent since Archmastery is rare and those who possess it arent always the most available or helpful sources</li> </ul></li> <li>How many successes are required and what vulgarity<ul><li>I would argue Vulgar and minimum 10 successes (probably more) since that is the base they mention for Gilgul and I would think fixing an Avatar is far more difficult than destroying one</li> </ul></li> <li>If its possible, should it succeed what happens to the Mage afterwards<ul><li>They might remain a Mage with a now healed Avatar</li> <li>The process might kill them (the sidebar regarding Cauls mentions that its believed it cannot be undone within one lifetime), their healed Avatar going on to be reincarnated</li> <li>They might lose points in 'mystical' strength (Avatar background, Arete, Spheres) from the ordeal their Avatar went through</li> <li>They might return to being an unawakened human, the process of repairing the Avatar having forced their awakened will back to sleep (if so you would have to determine if they could awaken again and if they do are they back to square one or can they quickly regain their former knowledge</li> <li>Depending on what Spheres you used (or didnt use) the Mage might still be haunted by what occurred (possibly gaining the PTSD flaw or a derangement)</li> <li>Can they be re-Cauled? (I would argue no since the Avatar having gone through the experience would likely kill the Mage and reincarnate than go through that hell again, if the Mage is dumb enough to fall prey again then they suffer the consequence of such stupidity)</li> </ul></li> <li>Likely the former Nephandi's dark master and its servants will not be happy losing one of their pieces and will take action</li> </ul><br /> No matter what it should be a game changing experience for all the Mages involved and should knowledge of their deed (success or failure) become known they will find themselves attracting a great deal of interest. Undoing the Caul could be the capstone journey on a long running Mage chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:29:05-07:00","id":989485,"title":"","content":"On that kind of stuff, there is no way I would submit it to the game system ^^<br /> <br /> In that sort of scenari, I tend to let the players decide the end. Well... not completely true. I get to decide how it ends, but I do it accordingly to their actions. If the point of the scenario is a big ritual, we work on making a good description, but most of the time, they did many things to prepare so I would not let the end be decided by a roll. This is too frustrating for some players (at least the ones I met before). How do I choose in the end woud you ask me ? Well, I go for the most dramatic end possible to close the session on something like an apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Oh, of course, they will have to search for the right Spheres and everything, they would have too describe the long ritual because many successes would be needed, but in the end, there is little chance that I make them roll the ritual. Of course, there are some exceptions but in this case, I would not.<br /> <br /> I have the experience of the Red Sign, which is an official setting of a cross story between Mages and Vampires. The point was to discover the ritual of the Red Sign that was supposed to make a Vampire human again (I would not give the details here but your demand ^^). There is no description of the ritual itself in the setting to let everyone play it the way they want. I decided to go for a table with the True Name of Uriel written in forgotten langage. Uriel cursed the vampires in the first place in the name of God and my ritual was about calling him to give back the soul and the human condition of one of the vampires. We were two STs for that and we had 8 players (4 Mages and 4 Vampires). The characters were old and powerful enough to perform the ritual they spend years searching (in game time of course).<br /> <br /> In the end, many rituals were performed and rolled:<br /> - The powerful Wards to hold Uriel hostage,<br /> - The search of the lost soul of the Vampire in the Low Umbra,<br /> - The protective spell that shielded the vampires from the holly fire of the Archangel to make possible the encounter,<br /> - etc...<br /> These rituals were all Magick spells, thaumaturgy and necromancy and they rolled most of them. But in the end, I did not decide the end of the scenario on rolls. I did not let them roll the actual call of Uriel. The scenario would have fallen flat if they had missed. So I said they succeded and we role-played the scene with the Archangel. Then of course, they delt with the consequences (nasty nasty ones).<br /> <br /> Well, my point was to say that in most dramatic moments, when cosmic forces are in action, I do not advise rolling anything for the risk of killing the interest of the scenario is too great. However, had they failed one of the necessary previous prep-rituals, I was prepared to make the encounter go wrong (the wards could not contain the holly being, the sun-shield was not powerful enough, the lost sould was a corrupted spirit, ...). See what I mean ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}